// Snippet: Options
// Pattern: insult sword-fight duel (classic pirate banter)
// Features: options, once-options, guarded options ($sword_skill),
//            <<if>> / <<elseif>> / <<else>>, <<jump>> for one-way transitions
// Run: cargo run -p bubbles-tui -- examples/snippets/options.bub

title: Start
---
<<declare $sword_skill = 2>>

Duelist: I challenge you to a duel of wits and blades, stranger!
Duelist: Let's see if your tongue is as sharp as your cutlass.

-> once Ask for the ground rules.
    Duelist: We trade insults first. Draw steel only if your wit fails.
    Duelist: Ask again and I'll know you're stalling.
-> Deliver a devastating insult. <<if $sword_skill >= 3>>
    You: Your sword arm is as weak as a soggy biscuit!
    Duelist: ...
    Duelist: I have no response to that. Well played.
    <<jump Victory>>
-> Stall for time.
    You: Before we begin... did you know your boots are on the wrong feet?
    Duelist: They are not - wait, are they?
    <<jump Escaped>>
-> Surrender immediately.
    You: I yield! Take whatever you want.
    Duelist: Hm. That was... disappointingly easy.
    <<jump Defeated>>
===

title: Victory
---
Bystander: That was the quickest duel I've ever seen.
===

title: Escaped
---
Bystander: Smart move. That fellow never wins a duel either way.
===

title: Defeated
---
Duelist: I shall take your hat as a trophy.
You: Not the hat.
===
